.SS "virtual string SystemEx\&.AI\&.Backend\&.WebAIBackend< T >\&.OnCreateURL (WebAIBackendPayload< T > payload)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
Creates the final URL used for the HTTP request\&. This method is \fRvirtual\fP so that derived backends may customize how the request URL is constructed\&. Typical use cases include:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Appending query parameters
.IP "\(bu" 2
Switching between multiple endpoints
.IP "\(bu" 2
Adding API keys or version identifiers
.IP "\(bu" 2
Routing based on payload content
.PP

.PP
The default implementation simply returns \fBWebAIBackendPayload<T>\&.URL\fP, making the backend functional without requiring subclass overrides\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpayload\fP The payload that will be sent to the backend\&. This may contain additional information that derived classes can use to construct dynamic URLs\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The fully constructed URL used for the HTTP POST request\&. 
.RE
.PP

